        items: [
          { zh: "央行決定維持利率不變，以免進一步打擊疲弱的經濟。", en: "The central bank decided to keep interest rates unchanged so as not to further weaken the fragile economy.", alt: ["The central bank decided to keep interest rates unchanged to avoid further weakening the fragile economy.", "The central bank decided to leave interest rates unchanged so as not to further weaken the fragile economy.", "The central bank decided to hold interest rates steady so as not to further weaken the weak economy."], note: "so as not to + V = 以免…" },
          { zh: "通膨侵蝕了一般家庭的購買力，尤其是低收入家庭。", en: "Inflation has eroded the purchasing power of ordinary households, especially low-income ones.", alt: ["Inflation has eroded the purchasing power of ordinary households, particularly low-income ones.", "Inflation has eroded the purchasing power of ordinary households, especially low-income households.", "Inflation has eaten into the purchasing power of ordinary households, especially low-income ones."], note: "ones 代替前面的 households；low-income 加連字號" },
          { zh: "分散投資雖然無法消除風險，卻能大幅降低整體波動。", en: "Although diversification can't eliminate risk, it can significantly reduce overall volatility.", alt: ["While diversification can't eliminate risk, it can significantly reduce overall volatility.", "Diversification can't eliminate risk, but it can significantly reduce overall volatility.", "Although diversification cannot eliminate risk, it can greatly reduce overall volatility."], note: "eliminate = 消除；volatility = 波動" },
          { zh: "消息一傳出，股市應聲下跌，投資人紛紛拋售科技股。", en: "As soon as the news broke, the stock market fell, and investors rushed to sell off tech stocks.", alt: ["As soon as the news broke, the stock market fell and investors rushed to sell off tech stocks.", "The stock market fell as soon as the news broke, with investors rushing to sell off tech stocks.", "As soon as the news broke, stocks fell, and investors rushed to sell off tech shares."], note: "the news broke = 消息傳出；with + 受詞 + V-ing（附帶狀況）" },
          { zh: "供應鏈中斷推高了生產成本，最終轉嫁到消費者身上。", en: "Supply chain disruptions have driven up production costs, which are ultimately passed on to consumers.", alt: ["Supply chain disruptions have pushed up production costs, which are ultimately passed on to consumers.", "Supply chain disruptions have driven up production costs, which have ultimately been passed on to consumers.", "Disruptions in the supply chain have driven up production costs, which are ultimately passed on to consumers."], note: "pass on to = 轉嫁給；which 指 costs" },
          { zh: "這家新創公司在最近一輪融資中募得五千萬美元，估值翻了一倍。", en: "The startup raised $50 million in its latest funding round, doubling its valuation.", alt: ["The startup raised fifty million dollars in its latest funding round, doubling its valuation.", "The startup raised $50 million in its latest round of funding, doubling its valuation.", "The startup raised $50 million in its latest funding round, and its valuation doubled."], note: "分詞構句 doubling… 表示結果" },
          { zh: "這家公司的現金流不足以償還債務，因此可能被迫出售部分資產。", en: "The company's cash flow is insufficient to repay its debts, so it may be forced to sell some of its assets.", alt: ["The company's cash flow is insufficient to repay its debts, so it may have to sell some of its assets.", "The company's cash flow isn't enough to repay its debts, so it may be forced to sell some of its assets.", "The company's cash flow is insufficient to repay its debt, so it might be forced to sell some of its assets."], note: "be forced to = 被迫；insufficient to V = 不足以" },
          { zh: "貨幣貶值雖然有利出口，卻會推高進口成本、加劇通膨壓力。", en: "Although currency depreciation benefits exports, it drives up import costs and adds to inflationary pressure.", alt: ["While currency depreciation benefits exports, it drives up import costs and adds to inflationary pressure.", "Although currency depreciation helps exports, it drives up import costs and adds to inflationary pressure.", "Currency depreciation benefits exports, but it drives up import costs and adds to inflationary pressure."], note: "add to = 加劇；inflationary pressure = 通膨壓力" },
          { zh: "經濟學家預測明年將出現溫和衰退，但就業市場應該能保持穩定。", en: "Economists predict a mild recession next year, but the job market should remain stable.", alt: ["Economists are predicting a mild recession next year, but the job market should remain stable.", "Economists forecast a mild recession next year, but the job market should remain stable.", "Economists predict a mild recession next year, but the job market should stay stable."], note: "should remain = 應該會維持（推測）" },
          { zh: "高槓桿的策略在牛市中報酬驚人，但在熊市中可能讓你血本無歸。", en: "Highly leveraged strategies can deliver huge returns in a bull market but wipe you out in a bear market.", alt: ["Highly leveraged strategies can deliver huge returns in a bull market, but they can wipe you out in a bear market.", "Highly leveraged strategies can bring huge returns in a bull market but wipe you out in a bear market.", "Highly leveraged investment strategies can deliver huge returns in a bull market but wipe you out in a bear market."], note: "bull market = 牛市、bear market = 熊市；wipe out = 讓人血本無歸" },
          { zh: "要不是政府及時介入，整個金融體系可能早就崩潰了。", en: "Had the government not intervened in time, the entire financial system might have collapsed.", alt: ["If the government hadn't intervened in time, the entire financial system might have collapsed.", "If the government had not stepped in in time, the whole financial system could have collapsed.", "Had the government not stepped in in time, the entire financial system might have collapsed."], note: "Had + 主詞 + not + 過去分詞 = If … had not…（倒裝）" },
          { zh: "我們不應該把所有雞蛋放在同一個籃子裡，尤其是在市場這麼不穩的時候。", en: "We shouldn't put all our eggs in one basket, especially when the market is so volatile.", alt: ["We shouldn't put all our eggs in one basket, especially when the market is so unstable.", "We shouldn't put all of our eggs in one basket, especially when the market is so volatile.", "We shouldn't put all our eggs in one basket, particularly when the market is so volatile."], note: "put all your eggs in one basket = 孤注一擲" }
        ]
